  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 159 AM MST Mon Nov 2 2026/ \n\nPrecipitation is already diminishing from west to east, but the \ntrough axis looks to send a couple more shortwaves that will lower\nH700 temperatures to around -5C through the early morning hours. \nLingering snow will be most widespread over and near the \nMadison/Gallatin Ranges and the Little Belt/Snowies in central MT.\nThere may also be some patchy fog development for wind protected \nareas that happen to clear out prior to or near sunrise. Gusty \nnorthwesterly surface winds on the backside of the departing \ntrough will continue through the day, with the eastern portion of \ncentral/north-central MT looking to see wind speeds exceeding the \n25 to 30 mph ranges at times. \n\nEnsembles continue to favor ridging aloft to bring milder and \ndrier conditions heading into the mid-week period; however, breezy\nconditions develop on Tuesday in advance of weak shortwave, \nfollowed by a brief and modest cooldown on Wednesday. A more \nprogressive pattern becomes established over the Northern Rockies \nduring the second half of the week and brings breezy to windy \nconditions and mostly mountain precipitation for the weekend. \n- RCG",
